---
import StaticLayout from "@/components/static/StaticLayout.astro";
import GreetingText from "@/components/dynamic/GreetingText";

const birthday = 1117650600;
const currentTime = Date.now() / 1000;
const age = Math.floor((currentTime - birthday) / (365.25 * 24 * 3600));
---

<StaticLayout
	title="Angad Bhalla"
	description="Software engineer building systems, backend tools, and thoughtful experiences."
	canonicalPath="/"
>
	<main class="space-y-8 py-8 sm:py-12">
		<section class="items-center justify-center p-6 sm:p-8">
			<p class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-white/45">
				<GreetingText initial="Hello!" client:visible />
			</p>
			<h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
				I'm Angad Bhalla
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-white/70">
				I'm {age}. I like playing Minecraft, watching Marvel &amp; DC,
				drinking coffee and building cool things for me and my friends.
				I'm also lactose intolerant.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="philosophy" class="p-6 sm:p-8">
			<p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-white/40">
				My Philosophy
			</p>
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">
				On Building Things
			</h2>
			<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-sm leading-8 text-white/70">
				<p>
					I think the best engineers treat software the same way a craftsman
					treats his work. Every project is another chance to create something
					beautiful, and the best way to learn is to make mistakes.
				</p>
				<p>
					The most fun projects tend to start with a "I know this sounds weird
					but what if-" and the best ones are the ones where you don't know
					yet what the final product will be.
				</p>
				<p>
					The goofier the project, the better.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</StaticLayout>